# A0-07 validation evidence

status: passed
revision: 1

The three independently reported fail-opens were reproduced before correction as `allow=true` with an empty deny set. After correction, the same missing-boolean, malformed-boolean, and minimal caller-shaped approval cases all return `allow=false` with a non-empty closed reason. The valid canonical A0-06 approval path remains reachable.

The SPEC check programmatically validates the closed persistent-artifact JSON Schema; closed typed catalog rows including missing/malformed booleans, extra fields, malformed/duplicate roles, identical duplicate rows, split witnesses, and ambiguity; canonical A0-06 approval schema and integrity including requester/approver, chronology, expiry, unconsumed state, every binding, and the closed egress authorization context; every documented policy output; and canonical-reference uniqueness.

## Fail-open reproduction before correction

```text
missing requires_approval: {"allow":true,"deny_reason":[]}
malformed requires_approval="yes": {"allow":true,"deny_reason":[]}
minimal caller-shaped approval: {"allow":true,"deny_reason":[]}
```

